Phase 6 (NeoTest Assessment) is complete. Key findings:

- **Clock 1 (R&D): 0 years** — no pull precedent has accelerated invention; CARB-X already funds candidates with push capital
- **Clock 2 (first-LMIC): 2–3 years** (range 1–5) — the pull can compress price-negotiation and procurement routing, but cannot compress clinical evidence generation or WHO-PQ category creation
- **Clock 3 (rollout): 1–2 years** (range 0–3) — no Gavi-equivalent delivery platform exists for diagnostics
- **Composite: ~3 years** (range 1–5) — equals the pull-only median from the cross-case distribution
- **7 years exceeds the pull-only maximum** (6 years, HPV vaccine with Gavi platform) and is **2× the precedent-calibrated central estimate**
- Replacing 7yr with 3yr worsens $/DALY by ~2.3×

